      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "William George Patterson bought land with three springs, hoping their healing powers would cure his son, and built a 30‑to‑40 room resort for travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patterson_Springs%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The resort attracted visitors from North Carolina, South Carolina, and Georgia, and when guests rested it offered lawn bowling and Saturday night dances.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patterson_Springs%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A single school building served all eleven grades in 1915, but the post office closed in the 1960s and both schools shut down in the 1970s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
